  "content": {
    "title": "Chipotle's Friday the 13th freebie gets those with tattoos a BOGO deal",
    "text": "March 12, 2026, 3:00 p.m. ETYour tattoo can get you a deal at Chipotle on Friday the 13th.Actually, you don't even have to have a real tattoo. Visit Chipotle with any temporary tattoo or drawn-on tattoo on March 13 from 3 p.m. to 4 p.m. local time and you can buy one entrée and get one free.The tattoo BOGO deal has some timely inspiration. Friday the 13th has become a day when tattoo shops often have price reductions, leading customers to opt for ink on that day. And there's that internet meme of folks being \"tatted like a Chipotle bag\" – it arose because the Chipotle bag has tattoo-styled iconography on the sides, similar to the look achieved by some tattoo diehards.\"What started as an internet meme became a real-world expression of fandom for our brand,\" said Stephanie Perdue, Chipotle's interim chief marketing officer, in a news release.This year, the Mexican-casual chain is partnering with Swae Lee, a heavily tattooed singer known for rap duo Rae Sremmurd and who has his solo debut album, \"Same Difference,\" out April 3. Lee helped with the creation of a sheet of temporary tattoos inspired by Chipotle's takeout bags that will be handed out for free on March 13 at the Midtown Miami restaurant (3201 N. Miami Ave., Miami, Florida).\"'Tatted like a Chipotle bag' is really about self-expression,\" Swae Lee said in a statement. \"It was cool to bring it into the real world and create designs that actually feel like me.\"How to buy one, get one free entrée at Chipotle on March 13To get the BOGO, dine in at Chipotle on Friday, March 13, from 3 p.m. to 4 p.m. local time and show off your tattoo, whether it’s permanent, temporary or even a drawn-on design, to unlock the BOGO. (Qualification will be determined at the sole discretion of restaurant staff, Chipotle says.)The buy-one-get-one (BOGO) promotion is limited to five free menu items per check (each free item must be matched by a purchased item of equal or greater value). However, each freebie needs to be collected by a person with a tattoo. So, a check with five free items would need to be picked up by five friends, each of whom has some type of tattoo.\"Bringing this promotion back for Friday the 13th further establishes our connection with the tattoo community, and partnering with Swae Lee allows us to spotlight his authentic passion for the brand and give our fans something extra to commemorate the moment together,\" Perdue said.Mike Snider is a national trending news reporter for USA TODAY. You can follow him on Threads, Bluesky, X and email him at mikegsnider & @mikegsnider.bsky.social & @mikesnider & msnider@usatoday.com.",
